  |title I think you just committed all of Resonance's in-progress work accidentally

  |quote
    I think you just committed all of Resonance's in-progress work accidentally. We should be more careful and not commit things we didn't change :-)

  |occasion
    Caught in the moment, immediately after the commit happened, named plainly
    and specifically (whose work, what happened) rather than as a general
    reminder to be careful.

  |about
    A correction stated as a shared standard going forward ("we should be more
    careful") rather than as blame at the agent who ran the command, with the
    smiley softening the delivery without softening the correction itself.

    No counter-virtue for this specific weakness (git-scope carefulness before
    committing) turned up in this pass — searched around "commit," "careful,"
    and adjacent phrasing without finding a demonstrated instance of the other
    half. Noting the absence rather than manufacturing a pair for it, per the
    brief's own instruction.

  |should-come-to-mind-when
    - You are about to run a commit after touching files you did not intend to
      change, or after a broad `git add`.
    - You are reviewing someone else's git action and see something that looks
      like scope creep — name it specifically, not as a general caution.
